  "spec": ["REH 4.3", "REH 4.5", "residential 7.1"],
  "description": "REH 4.3: GetOrdinanceEffects at Init and, after clearing both lists, in every state 0: one element per service and ordinance (ascending ID) that has at least one of its six properties. 0x10: school radius 50, capacity 200, effect 110 and decay 50 %; 0x11: health effect 110 and decay 200 %; 0x12: only a school age curve (a curve alone makes an element, with the factors at 1.0); 0x13: no effect property (no element); 0x14: school effect 110. School (m1, m2, m3) = (0.5, 2.0, 1.1f x 1.0 x 1.1f = 1.21 = 0x3F9AE148), health (1, 1, 1.1); decay products (0.5, 2.0), which scale the EQ and HQ decays when the population tuning is re-read in state 4 (0.2 x 0.5 = 0.1, 0.2 x 2 = 0.4). With 0x14 off, state 0 re-reads 2 school elements (m3 1.1). Grading a school of capacity 1000 over 8000 residents: 0x12's age curve (50) halves the served population (ma = (50 x ma) x 0.01) to 4000, and m2 = 2 makes the effective capacity 2000: grade and staff ratio 0.5.",
  "steps": [
    {"op": "residential_env", "ordinances": {"0x10": {"0xA91B3AF4": {"f32": 50}, "0x892D9D02": {"f32": 200}, "0xA92D9D7A": {"f32": 110}, "0x692EF65A": {"f32": 50}}, "0x11": {"0xE91B3AEE": {"f32": 110}, "0xC92D9C7A": {"f32": 200}}, "0x12": {"0xC91B3B02": {"f32": [0, 50, 100, 50]}}, "0x13": {"0x12345678": {"u32": 7}}, "0x14": {"0xA92D9D7A": {"f32": 110}}}},
    {"op": "residential_env", "groups": {"1": ["0x150F"]}, "props": {"1": {"0x8922041B": {"u32": 1000}, "0x691B42B3": {"f32": 10}}}, "lots": {"1": [32, 32]}},
    {"op": "residential_create"},
